# Next.js Web Conventions

## App Router
- Use App Router (`app/` directory). Server Components by default; `'use client'` only when needed.
- Route groups: `(storefront)`, `(b2b-portal)`, `(my-garage)`, `(admin)`.
- API routes under `app/api/v1/` — thin handlers delegating to `packages/shared/` logic.

## Performance (Visual Parts Catalog)
- Diagram images: use `next/image` with WebP/AVIF, lazy loading, and blur placeholders.
- Interactive canvas: render base diagram as `<img>` with absolutely-positioned SVG/bounding-box overlays.
- Bounding boxes from `part_fitment` spatial data — highlight on hover, open add-to-cart modal on click.
- Search: delegate to Meilisearch/PostgreSQL FTS via `/api/v1/store/search` — support 4-way search (part number, VIN, model variant, PNC category).

## Multi-Currency Display
- Always show currency alongside amounts. Dual USD/ZiG display where ContiPay settlement requires it.
- Never assume USD — read `currency` field from API responses.

## State Management
- Server state: React Query / TanStack Query with Supabase client.
- Client state: Zustand or React Context for cart, active garage vehicle, UI preferences.
- "My Garage" vehicle selection silently filters all search paths to fitment-compatible parts.

## Styling
- Use design tokens from `packages/ui/`. Invoke `/ui-ux-pro-max` skill for intentional typography/color/motion.
- Mobile-first responsive design. Catalog canvas must work on tablet and desktop.

## Security
- No service_role key in client bundles. All data access through RLS-protected Supabase queries.
- No HTML5 QR scanning — web app does not scan QR codes (mobile bridges only).
